proposals.what:
`UI.fact(el, key, args)` (F1 kit) turns a displayed number into a button: a dotted underline on hover devices, no visual change on touch. Tap or Enter opens a popover (a bottom sheet under 760px) with:
- the value and a one-line definition;
- the arithmetic with the student's own numbers;
- what was included and left out, with counts;
- `See the rows`, linking to the filtered list (Review History, Results sittings, the calendar day);
- `Same number on: Today · Me · Results`.

`GET /api/fact/{key}` (F4) covers `streak`, `minutes?period`, `accuracy?topic&window`, `mastery?topic`, `estimate`, `percentile?sid`, `points?topic|trap`, `open_mistakes`, `rank?metric&period&scope` and `pace?sid`. Each calls the very function the pages display from (one source, rule 5). It returns `{value, label, formula_text, parts:[{label,n}], excluded:[{label,n}], href}`.

Examples:
- Accuracy 72%: '131 right of 182 first tries in the last 30 days. Left out: 14 exact repeats, 3 disputed. 4 right guesses count half.'
- Streak 6: '6 study days in a row (an answer, 10 word reviews or a finished sitting). Sat and Sun were plan rest days, so they kept it.'
- Estimate 560–650: 'Mean of your last 3 scored sittings within 45 days: 590, 610, 620. Confidence medium: only modules so far; a full section would tighten it.'

Applied to hero chips, Me's tiles, nav-meta tooltips, score cards, skill rows, report tiles, your leaderboard row and the plan's stat tiles.

For a learner with 0 answers, Today's Up next is `Start with 8 questions · about 10 min`, with the helper `One from each part of SAT Math, then four that adapt to you. No sign-up.` Enter starts it.

`POST /api/drill {count:8, mix:'blueprint', adaptive:true, source:'warmup'}` serves one medium question per domain, then 4 adaptive ones (up a tier after a right, down after a miss).

The summary variant `warmup` shows:
- four domain bars (`Algebra 2 of 2 · Advanced Math 1 of 3 …`) labelled `from 8 answers · rough`;
- the named mistakes opened, with `Fix now · 4 q`;
- the coach's next set;
- `Want a score range? One module · 22 q · 35 min`;
- a non-blocking `Save your progress`.

It shows no invented score. Afterwards every Today card has content: the Review card lists the new mistakes, study time shows 10 min, and the streak reads `Day 1`. The plan CTA preview uses the domain bars, and Plan step 1's SourceNote reads `8 practice answers · take a module for a real start`. A visitor who does anything else is never nagged, and Up next falls back to the coach's `new` pick.
